    "slug": "buying-holiday-home-portugal-post-completion-checklist",
    "date": "2026-02-06",
    "author": "Hugo Gonçalves",
    "content": "Completion is a legal milestone, but it is also the point at which practical responsibility for the property becomes yours. Before returning abroad, create a usable record of the home.\n\n## Inventory every means of access\n\nCount front-door, secondary-door, mailbox and garage keys, gate controls and alarm fobs. Test them and record any missing or unreliable item. Consider changing locks where key history is uncertain.\n\n## Photograph condition\n\nCreate clear photographs of rooms, walls, ceilings, equipment and external areas. Note visible defects separately so later changes can be identified. This is a practical baseline, not a substitute for a professional building survey.\n\n## Record systems and readings\n\nPhotograph utility meters and identify water controls, the consumer board, hot-water equipment, air-conditioning, internet equipment, pool systems and irrigation controls. Gather manuals and service records where available.\n\n## Build the contact file\n\nKeep condominium, alarm, insurance, pool, garden and trusted technical contacts together. Confirm who may access the property and how work will be authorised whilst you are abroad.\n\n## Put care in place before leaving\n\nChoose an inspection schedule, document how systems should be left and arrange the first visit. Guardemar’s [property handover service](/property-handover-algarve/) can lead directly into ongoing [private property care](/property-care/).",
